  "body": "**Suggestion**\r\nAs the admin of a homeserver it would be nice to have a kind of \"Report\" message. This way clients could implement a \"report\" button which then sends a notification to the room's moderators (for which notifications can be handled differently from a simple ping). As another step for escalation, it might also be useful to add a \"Report to Server Administrators\" for illegal content, so it can be purged from from media repositories.\r\n\r\nSo to put it in not-wall-of-text-form:\r\n- add a report message type `m.report` which can be sent to notify moderators without filling the history with pings\r\n    - by default the report messages should only be displayed to people of a certain powerlevel\r\n    - Example:\r\n      ```xml\r\n      <mx-report>\r\n      @user:homeserver.tld has reported https://matrix.to/#/%21WjNnPFIjXXXXXXXXXX%3Amatrix.org/%24nBSjBXVXXXXXXXXXX-eHBcWnlaqfZYJpVXXXXXXXXXXX\r\n      reason: I find this distasteful\r\n      </mx-report>\r\n      ```\r\n- add a report message type `m.escalate` which can be sent from a certain powerlevel to notify server administrators of messages\r\n    - escalation messages are handled by the server (sent as an email, sent to a dedicated room, etc.)\r\n\r\nLimitations:\r\n- admin-notification obviously only works in unencrypted rooms\r\n- admins might be exposed to disgusting shit\r\n- might be abused to spam admins and moderators (the latter can take appropriate action in their rooms, for the former I don't have a \"simple\" solution at hand)\r\n- servers have to implement the escalation functionality",
